-- title:
--   Level field of the full-level model is a function field in j
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero $M'$, and write $F =$ `fieldBar q M'` for the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ with $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, realised as an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $K_1$ an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_1/k_0$ finite; give $F$ its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $F_0$ be a $k_0$-subextension of $F$, and put $L_1 = k_0(\mathrm{image\ of\ }K_1) \sqcup F_0$, the join inside $F$ of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$. Assume: the join of $k_0(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ with $F_0$ is all of $F$; for every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ that is $K_1$-linearly independent and every family $a$ of elements of $L_1$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ in $F$ forces $a = 0$; and every element of $F$ whose Laurent series has coefficients in $\mathbb Q$ lies in $F_0$. Assume further given a $K_1$-algebra structure on $L_1$ whose structure map agrees with $K_1 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \to F$. Then for any $j_1 \in L_1$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$, the element $j_1$ is transcendental over $K_1$ and $L_1$ is finite-dimensional over $K_1(j_1)$.
--
--   This is the statement that the level field $K_1F_0$ of the full-level model of $X_H(q^2M')$ is a one-variable function field with the modular invariant $j$ as a transcendence generator, in the form needed for descent of the model from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to the finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$. It is the input to the descent lemmas that produce polynomial relations over $k_0$ satisfied by coordinates on the model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_transcendental_and_finiteDimensional_adjoin_levelField.lean

